# Ticket 45 (#180): optional /opt/cmp/.env lines for the demo analysis·Sandbox·Claude runtime.
# Copy only what you turn on into /opt/cmp/.env (root, 0600) in an SSM session, then release.
# Never commit real values. Keys ensure-secrets.sh generates (ENV_FILE_ENCRYPTION_KEY, …) are
# not listed here; build values (PLATFORM_ECR_REGISTRY, BUILD_*) come from deploy-build-stack.sh.
#
# Real analysis. Both lines → the analysis queue registers the real Activities (dict input) and
# the web (`target`) start analyses for real. The scaffold start (no `target`) then fails in
# analysis: one worker serves one path. The store must equal ARTIFACT_STORE_DIR.
ANALYSIS_ARTIFACT_STORE_DIR=/opt/cmp/artifact-store
ANALYSIS_WORKSPACE_ROOT=/opt/cmp/analysis-workspaces
#
# Real Sandbox loop (박승철님 값, 협의 필요). Place the dedicated `k3d-cmp-sandbox` kubeconfig at
# /opt/cmp/secrets/sandbox/kubeconfig (root, 0600) first, then SANDBOX_KUBECONFIG=/run/cmp/sandbox/kubeconfig.
# Empty: scaffold Sandbox; a real (`target`) start then stops at sbx_build.
SANDBOX_KUBECONFIG=
# JSON {"<resource id>": "<repo>@sha256:<digest>"} until all BUILD_* are set (runbook).
SANDBOX_PREBUILT_IMAGES=
#
# Claude (ADR-004, 협의 필요: 비용 한도·키 소유). Off unless true and a key is set.
LLM_ENABLED=false
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# Agent chat on the platform (`POST /agent/ask`, the web server calls it): off unless true. It uses the
# same ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and spend ledger as above (one budget, one kill switch). AGENT_CHAT_MODEL
# defaults to claude-haiku-5-5; AGENT_CHAT_CAPTION_MODEL (screen-language caption) defaults to it.
AGENT_CHAT_ENABLED=false
#
# Ticket 57 (#228): the rehearsal's standard write -> read shape for web starts (API only), a
# SandboxSettings JSON object. This line is the demo app (demo-app main.go): POST /api/messages
# answers 201 with a server-made `id`; the same client_msg_id again answers 200 with the stored
# row, so the read-back is REPEAT_WRITE. Keep the single quotes (compose reads the JSON
# literally). Empty: the rehearsal runs the health test only. Another app needs its own shape.
WEB_START_SANDBOX_SETTINGS='{"write_path": "/api/messages", "write_body": {"client_msg_id": "std-{{run_id}}", "author": "cmp-rehearsal", "body": "value-{{run_id}}"}, "write_status": 201, "id_from_response": "id", "value_field": "body", "read_back": "REPEAT_WRITE"}'
#
# Red-team attack-result cache (worker, optional). Reuses a past attack result when the same source is
# deployed again; the web start screen's toggle turns the reuse off per run. Empty bucket: no cache at all
# (the toggle then has no effect). Objects go to s3://<bucket>/[<prefix>/]redteam/attack/<source_sha256>/
# <ids|initial>.json . The instance role may only write under the state bucket's `cmp/` prefix (and the
# deploy bucket's sources/tests/builds), so the demo value is REDTEAM_CACHE_BUCKET=<the state bucket>,
# REDTEAM_CACHE_PREFIX=cmp (objects under cmp/redteam/). Another bucket or prefix needs an IAM change.
REDTEAM_CACHE_BUCKET=
REDTEAM_CACHE_PREFIX=
#
# Provisioning 72 (ADR-007 단계 6): the data-migration Activities' cluster access (worker). After
# deploy-data-migration-stack.sh and its DATA_MIGRATION_ROLE_ARN line, set
# DATA_MIGRATION_AWS_PROFILE=cmp-demo-data-migration. For a KUBECONFIG endpoint (on-prem k3d), put
# <kubeconfig_ref>.yaml under /opt/cmp/secrets/data-migration (root, 0600) and set
# DATA_MIGRATION_KUBECONFIG_DIR=/run/cmp/data-migration. Empty: that access fails closed.
DATA_MIGRATION_AWS_PROFILE=
DATA_MIGRATION_KUBECONFIG_DIR=
#
# Data-migration ticket 08: the data step's input for web starts (API only), a DataMigrationInput
# JSON object, the same value as `scripts/start_migration.py --data-migration`: source DbEndpoint,
# source app (namespace, deployment, url_secret), cutover settings (image) and the target tunnel
# address. No secrets. Keep the single quotes. Empty: the data step stays the scaffold. The value
# depends on the WireGuard path between the clusters, so it stays empty here.
# ON_PREM (ADR-007 2안, Provisioning 76) also sets `tunnel` (ingress "source", target_egress_cidrs
# = the laptop's public IP/32), `target_kubeconfig_ref` and `network_preflight` (aws_vpc_cidrs,
# db_auth_ref = Secret name/keys only). Ticket 82: tunnel "standing_ingress": true reuses the
# source NLB pre-created with `make data-tunnel-nlb-up`. See infra/demo/README.md.
WEB_START_DATA_MIGRATION=
#
# #128: the traffic step's input for web starts (API only), a TrafficShiftInput JSON object, the
# same value as `scripts/start_migration.py --traffic`: the relay server's worker queue and the
# step policy. No secrets. Keep the single quotes. Empty: the traffic step stays the scaffold and
# the relay is never touched. Demo relay (`cmp-demo-relay`): relay_queue "relay-1".
WEB_START_TRAFFIC=
# Origin/target servers report CPU and memory to POST /system/pulse/report with this shared token.
# Empty = the endpoint is off. Generate a long random value; never commit it.
PULSE_REPORT_TOKEN=
